# Implementation Plan: Survey Builder Animation and UX Improvements

## Executive Summary

This plan outlines the implementation of three key UX improvements to the survey builder:
1. **Better Drop Area Visualization** - Enhanced drop indicator with clearer visual feedback
2. **Animated Item Movement** - Smooth animations when items move to make space for drops
3. **Visible Delete Button** - Direct delete button on question cards

---

## Current Architecture Analysis

### Drag-and-Drop Flow
The survey builder uses `@dnd-kit/core` for cross-container drag operations and `@dnd-kit/sortable` for reordering within the canvas. The state management flows through:

1. **`index.tsx`** (SurveyBuilder) - Main DnD context, manages `activeDragItem` and `overId` state
2. **`builder-canvas.tsx`** - Receives `activeDragItem` and `overId` as props, renders questions with drop indicators
3. **`question-card.tsx`** - Individual draggable/sortable question cards

### Current Drop Indicator Behavior
- Located in `builder-canvas.tsx` (lines 34-52)
- Shows a dashed border box with "Drop to add question here" text
- Appears at the calculated drop position when `isOver` is true and `activeDragItem?.type === "palette"`
- Uses `AnimatePresence` for enter/exit animations

### Current Animation Patterns
- Uses `framer-motion` throughout
- `motion.div` with spring animations for question cards
- `AnimatePresence` with `mode="popLayout"` for list transitions
- Individual cards have enter/exit animations but no layout animations for displacement

---

## Implementation Plan

### Task 1: Enhanced Drop Indicator with Better Visualization

**File:** `/apps/web/src/components/survey-builder/builder-canvas.tsx`

**Changes:**
1. Redesign `DropIndicator` component with more prominent visual feedback
2. Add animated glow/pulse effect to indicate drop zone
3. Include the question type being dragged in the indicator

**Key Code Changes:**

```tsx
// Enhanced DropIndicator component (replace lines 34-52)
interface DropIndicatorProps {
	questionType?: Question["type"];
}

function DropIndicator({ questionType }: DropIndicatorProps) {
	const questionTypeLabels: Record<string, string> = {
		text: "Short Text",
		textarea: "Long Text",
		multiple_choice: "Multiple Choice",
		// ... other types
	};

	return (
		<motion.div
			initial={{ opacity: 0, scale: 0.95, height: 0 }}
			animate={{ opacity: 1, scale: 1, height: "auto" }}
			exit={{ opacity: 0, scale: 0.95, height: 0 }}
			transition={{ 
				type: "spring", 
				stiffness: 400, 
				damping: 30,
				height: { duration: 0.2 }
			}}
			className="overflow-hidden"
		>
			<div className="relative flex min-h-[70px] items-center gap-3 rounded-xl border-2 border-violet-500 bg-gradient-to-r from-violet-50 to-purple-50 p-4 shadow-sm">
				{/* Animated glow ring */}
				<motion.div
					className="absolute inset-0 rounded-xl border-2 border-violet-400"
					animate={{ 
						opacity: [0.3, 0.7, 0.3],
						scale: [1, 1.02, 1]
					}}
					transition={{ 
						duration: 1.5, 
						repeat: Infinity,
						ease: "easeInOut"
					}}
				/>
				<div className="relative z-10 flex items-center gap-3 w-full">
					<div className="flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-violet-500 shadow-md">
						<Plus className="h-5 w-5 text-white" />
					</div>
					<div>
						<span className="font-semibold text-sm text-violet-700">
							Drop to add question here
						</span>
						{questionType && (
							<span className="ml-2 text-violet-500 text-xs">
								({questionTypeLabels[questionType] || questionType})
							</span>
						)}
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</motion.div>
	);
}
```

